  "guidance": "Updates outlook for full year 2024: Adjusted sales* of $79.25 - $79.75 billion, up from $78.75 - $79.5 billion; Adjusted EPS* of $5.50 - $5.58, up from $5.35 - $5.45; Confirms free cash flow* of approximately $4.7 billion.",
  "definitions": "Table 'Non-GAAP measure | Definition': Adjusted net sales - consolidated net sales (a GAAP measure), excluding net significant and/or non-recurring items (significant nonoperational items and/or significant operational items that may occur at irregular intervals). Organic sales - the change in consolidated net sales excluding the impact of foreign currency translation, acquisitions and divestitures completed in the preceding twelve months and net significant and/or non-recurring items. Adjusted operating profit (loss) and margin - operating profit (loss) excluding restructuring costs, acquisition accounting adjustments and net significant and/or non-recurring items; margin as a percentage of adjusted net sales. Segment operating profit (loss) and margin - operating profit (loss) excluding Acquisition Accounting Adjustments, the FAS/CAS operating adjustment, Corporate expenses and other unallocated items, and Eliminations and other. Adjusted segment sales - consolidated net sales excluding eliminations and other and net significant and/or non-recurring items. Adjusted segment operating profit (loss) and margin - segment operating profit (loss) excluding restructuring costs, and net significant and/or non-recurring items. Adjusted net income - net income (from continuing operations in the Q4-23 release) excluding restructuring costs, acquisition accounting adjustments and net significant and/or non-recurring items. Adjusted EPS - diluted EPS excluding the same items. Adjusted effective tax rate (from Q2-24) - the effective tax rate excluding the tax impact of restructuring costs, acquisition accounting adjustments and net significant and/or non-recurring items. Free cash flow - cash flow from operations less capital expenditures. Acquisition Accounting Adjustments include the amortization of acquired intangible assets, of the PP&E fair value adjustment, of customer contractual obligations related to loss making or below market contracts acquired, and goodwill impairment, if applicable. The FAS/CAS operating adjustment represents the difference between the service cost component of our pension and PRB expense under FAS and our pension and PRB expense under U.S. government CAS primarily related to our Raytheon segment. Non-GAAP Financial Adjustments table added (descriptions of each adjustment)."
 },
